# URL of the frontend application
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Limits per address need to know where a connection comes from. Set one of the two:
# - behind a proxy: the header the platform puts the client address in. On Render use cf-connecting-ip:
#   it holds one address and a client cannot set it. Do not use x-forwarded-for there: its last entry is an
#   internal address of the platform, so every player would look the same.
#   When the header holds a list, only the last entry is used, and it is only right if the proxy writes it.
# - without a proxy, or in local development: use the address of the connection itself.
#   Never behind a proxy: every player would look like the proxy and share one small limit.
# With neither, the limits per address are off and a warning is logged at start-up.
# CLIENT_IP_HEADER=cf-connecting-ip
# LIMIT_BY_PEER_ADDRESS=true
